  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><title>Activity</title>
<para id="para-00001">Your teacher will give you a <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/65ade6cf04697521f26b3f3f779957e058748fdf">set of cards</link> that each contain a number. Decide whether each number is a possible input for the functions described here. Sort the cards into two groups: possible inputs and impossible inputs. Record your sorting decisions.</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    <para id="para-00002">The area of a square, in square centimeters, is a function of its side length, \(s\), in centimeters. The equation \(A(s) =s^2\) defines this function. 
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00003">Possible inputs:</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00004">Compare your answers:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00005">Possible inputs: \(9\), \(\frac35\), \(15\), \(0\), \(0.8\), \(4\), \(\frac{25}4\), \(0.001\), \(6.8\), \(72\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
