<exercise id="exer-00003">
  <problem id="prob-00003">
    <para id="para-00009">A tennis camp charges $40 per student for a full-day camp. The camp only runs if at least 5 students sign up, and it limits the enrollment to 16 campers a day. The amount of revenue, in dollars, that the tennis camp collects is a function of the number of students who enroll.
        The equation \(R(n)=40n\) defines this function. 
        
    </para>
